 Create a `test_my_module.py` file inside the `tests` directory:\n\n```python\n# test_my_module.py\n\nfrom my_package.my_module import add\n\ndef test_add():\n    assert add(2, 3) == 5\n    assert add(0, 0) == 0\n    assert add(-1, 1) == 0\n```\n\nHere's what this example does:\n\n1. The test file is named `test_my_module.py`, and it's located within the `tests` directory.\n2. We import the `add` function from `my_package.my_module`, assuming that your package is properly structured and that `my_module.py` contains the `add` function.\n3. We define a test function called `test_add`, where we use assertions to check if the `add` function behaves as expected for various inputs.\n\nTo run the tests using pytest, make sure you have pytest installed (you can install it using `pip install pytest`). Then, from the root directory of your package (where the `my_package` directory is located), run:\n\n```\npytest\n```\n\nThis command will discover and run all the tests in the `tests` directory and its subdirectories. In this case, it will execute the `test_add` function in `test_my_module.py` and report the results.","turn_id":"turn_000003"},"target_developer_prompt":{"create_time":1706099386.015073,"event_index":2,"role":"user","source_node_id":"aaa2fe37-d3db-4582-a62b-d165c3c2719f","source_parent_id":"38f0656f-ff26-4065-b01c-7d03ddef04ab","source_record_index":2,"text":"minimal example for a pytest test in the directory structure of a python package","turn_id":"turn_000002"}},"csv_extraction":{"context":[{"category":"context","evidence_spans":["minimal example for a pytest test in the directory structure of a python package"],"item_id":"context_1","normalized_text":"The task concerns a pytest test within the directory structure of a Python package.","source_roles":["user"],"source_turn_ids":["turn_000002"]}],"specificity":[{"category":"specificity","evidence_spans":["minimal example for a pytest test in the directory structure of a python package"],"item_id":"specificity_1"